<h2>Medical Emergencies 🚨</h2>
<blockquote>Emergency medical knowledge and protocols for Medical Emergencies.</blockquote>
<h3>Overview</h3>
<p>Medical Emergencies is a critical topic in emergency medical services. This note covers the essential knowledge, protocols, and practical skills needed for EMTs.</p>
<h3>Key Concepts</h3>
<h4>Assessment</h4>
<ul><li>Primary survey (ABCDE approach)</li><li>Vital signs evaluation</li><li>History gathering (SAMPLE, OPQRST)</li><li>Physical examination findings</li></ul>
<h4>Management</h4>
<ul><li>Immediate interventions</li><li>Pharmacological treatment (within EMT scope)</li><li>Non-pharmacological interventions</li><li>Transport considerations and destination decisions</li></ul>
<h4>Protocols</h4>
<ul><li>Indications and contraindications</li><li>Step-by-step procedures</li><li>Documentation requirements</li><li>Quality improvement metrics</li></ul>
<h3>Practical Skills</h3>
<h4>Equipment Needed</h4>
<ul><li>Essential equipment list</li><li>Optional but helpful tools</li><li>Backup equipment</li></ul>
<h4>Procedure Steps</h4>
<p>1. Prepare equipment and ensure scene safety</p>
<p>2. Perform primary assessment</p>
<p>3. Apply appropriate interventions</p>
<p>4. Monitor patient response</p>
<p>5. Document all actions and findings</p>
<h3>Special Considerations</h3>
<h4>Pediatric Patients</h4>
<ul><li>Age-specific modifications</li><li>Weight-based dosing (Broselow tape)</li><li>Communication strategies with parents</li><li>Common pediatric emergencies</li></ul>
<h4>Geriatric Patients</h4>
<ul><li>Atypical presentations</li><li>Polypharmacy considerations</li><li>Fragility and fall risk</li><li>Communication challenges</li></ul>
<h4>Documentation</h4>
<ul><li>Time of onset and discovery</li><li>Interventions performed with timestamps</li><li>Patient response to treatment</li><li>Vital signs trend</li><li>Handoff report (MIST format)</li></ul>
<h3>Related</h3>
<ul><li>[[EMS Study Plan]]</li><li>[[Patient Assessment Algorithm]]</li><li>[[MOC - Health-EMT]]</li></ul>
